b105b3ccba881271c1ad7cbb6cfff57a1aa72078.body:
Fix an overlap constant \(\epsilon\) with \(0<\epsilon<1/2\).  Then there is a constant \(C_\epsilon>0\) such that, for every \(n\ge1\), \(m\ge0\), and \(d\ge2\), the clipped derandomized Poisson-prefix inverse-count estimator
\[
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC}}_{n,m,d}
=
\sum_{r_0=0}^{M_0}\sum_{r_f=0}^{n_f+m_f}
\Pr\{\operatorname{Poi}(M_0/8)=r_0\}
\Pr\{\operatorname{Poi}((n_f+m_f)/8)=r_f\}
\,\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC,prefix}}_{n,m,d}(r_0,r_f)
\]
is measurable and satisfies
\[
\sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}}
\mathbb E_{\mathcal E_{n,m,d,\epsilon}(P)}
\left[
\left\{
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC}}_{n,m,d}-\tau(P)
\right\}^2
\right]
\le
C_\epsilon
\min\left\{
1,\frac1n+\frac{d^2}{(n+m)^2}
\right\},
\]
where \(\tau(P)\) is the average treatment effect functional in \(\cref{obj:def:ate-functional}\).  Consequently, for the minimax risk in \(\cref{obj:def:minimax-risk}\),
\[
R_\epsilon(n,m,d)
\le
C_\epsilon
\min\left\{
1,\frac1n+\frac{d^2}{(n+m)^2}
\right\}.
\]

e3f603b1ebd95b0719f60a19e9b59d5beefa2c4d.body:
For an overlap constant \(\epsilon\) and alphabet size \(d\), define
\[
\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}
:=
\Bigl\{
P\in\mathsf{Prob}\bigl([d]\times\{0,1\}^2\bigr):
d\ge2,\ 0<\epsilon<1/2,\ \text{\(P\) satisfies \(\cref{obj:ass:overlap}\)}
\Bigr\}.
\]

01f45ed58fe002d21f1bf80ffc190c793d48e938.body:
Define the minimax mean-squared risk by
\[
R_\epsilon(n,m,d)
:=
\inf_{T\in\mathcal T_{n,m,d}}
\sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}}
E_{P^{\otimes n}\otimes P_{XA}^{\otimes m}}
\!\left[\bigl(T-\tau(P)\bigr)^2\right],
\]
where \(\mathcal T_{n,m,d}\) is the class of estimators measurable with respect to the labeled sample and auxiliary sample.

44b62a062759c384eda308f556dd1b97a0ec786d.body:
Fix an overlap constant \(\epsilon\) with \(0<\epsilon<1/2\).  Then there is a constant \(C_\epsilon>0\) such that the following holds for every \(n\ge1\), \(m\ge0\), and \(d\ge2\).  Let
\[
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC}}_{n,m,d}(Z)
=
\sum_{r_0=0}^{M_0}\sum_{r_f=0}^{n_f+m_f}
\Pr\{\operatorname{Poi}(M_0/8)=r_0\}
\Pr\{\operatorname{Poi}((n_f+m_f)/8)=r_f\}
\,\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC,prefix}}_{n,m,d}(Z;r_0,r_f),
\]
where \(M_0,n_f,m_f\) are the block sizes used in \cref{obj:def:mixed-estimator-handle}.  This clipped derandomized Poisson-prefix inverse-count estimator is measurable and satisfies
\[
\sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}}
\mathbb E_{P^{\otimes n}\otimes P_{XA}^{\otimes m}}
\left[
\left\{
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC}}_{n,m,d}-\tau(P)
\right\}^2
\right]
\le
C_\epsilon
\min\left\{
1,\frac1n+\frac{d^2}{(n+m)^2}
\right\},
\]
with \(\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}\) as in \cref{obj:def:model-class} and \(\tau(P)\) as in \cref{obj:def:ate-functional}.  Consequently, for the minimax risk in \cref{obj:def:minimax-risk},
\[
R_\epsilon(n,m,d)
\le
C_\epsilon
\min\left\{
1,\frac1n+\frac{d^2}{(n+m)^2}
\right\}.
\]

