b812e6b68ef5bea8cb61ba48cbab7290ce86e98a.body:
Fix an overlap constant \(\epsilon\) with \(0<\epsilon<1/2\).  Then there is a constant \(C_\epsilon>0\) such that, for every pair of sample sizes \(n\ge1\) and \(m\ge0\) and every alphabet size \(d\ge2\), the following clipped derandomized inverse-count estimator is measurable:
\[
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC}}_{n,m,d}(Z)
=
\sum_{r_0=0}^{M_0}
\sum_{r_f=0}^{n_f+m_f}
\mathbb P\{\operatorname{Poi}(M_0/8)=r_0\}
\mathbb P\{\operatorname{Poi}((n_f+m_f)/8)=r_f\}
\,\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC,prefix}}_{n,m,d}(Z,r_0,r_f),
\]
where \(M_0=\lfloor n/3\rfloor\), \(n_p=\lfloor(n-M_0)/2\rfloor\), \(n_f=n-M_0-n_p\), \(m_p=\lfloor m/2\rfloor\), and \(m_f=m-m_p\) are the block sizes of \(\cref{obj:def:mixed-estimator-handle}\), and the prefix statistic is the sample-and-prefix-count statistic in \(\cref{obj:synth_5}\).  Moreover,
\[
\sup_{P\in\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}}
\mathbb E_{P^{\otimes n}\otimes P_{XA}^{\otimes m}}
\left[
\left\{
\widehat\tau^{\mathrm{IC}}_{n,m,d}-\tau(P)
\right\}^2
\right]
\le
C_\epsilon
\min\left\{
1,\frac1n+\frac{d^2}{(n+m)^2}
\right\}.
\]
Here \(\mathcal M_{d,\epsilon}\) is the overlap class in \(\cref{obj:def:model-class}\), \(\tau(P)\) is the average treatment effect functional in \(\cref{obj:def:ate-functional}\), and the expectation is under the independent labeled and auxiliary product law of \(\cref{obj:def:annotation-experiment}\).  Consequently, for the minimax risk in \(\cref{obj:def:minimax-risk}\),
\[
R_\epsilon(n,m,d)
\le
C_\epsilon
\min\left\{
1,\frac1n+\frac{d^2}{(n+m)^2}
\right\}.
\]

